{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics", "label": "ADR-016 Metric samples through the collector contract and the outbox", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-016-metric-samples-and-headline-metrics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics_metric_sample", "label": "MetricSample / CollectorResult.samples (collector 0.2.0)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-016-metric-samples-and-headline-metrics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A sample references its CI by CiRef (identity, not stored id) the way a relationship references an endpoint, so collectors never need stored ids. Go view carries Samples with omitempty so a 0.1.0 collector's result still parses."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics_metric_name_pattern", "label": "METRIC_NAME_PATTERN (<domain>.<object>.<measure>[_<unit>])", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-016-metric-samples-and-headline-metrics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics_layer_headline_metric", "label": "LAYER_HEADLINE_METRIC / HEADLINE_METRIC_NAMES (ci 0.2.0)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-016-metric-samples-and-headline-metrics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One headline metric per layer with unit and label from the contract; the unknown layer's lastSeenDays is derived by the API from observedAt, never sampled."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics_openmap_metric_sampled_event", "label": "openmap.metric.sampled event (event 0.2.0)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-016-metric-samples-and-headline-metrics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reconciler resolves sample refs to CI ids (new CIs of the same result included), drops unresolvable samples (not parked; next sweep samples again), batches at most RECONCILER.samplesPerEvent per event. Outbox row pending for ClickHouse only; no graph node, search document or live update carries a sample."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics_metrics_latest", "label": "ClickHouse metrics_latest (ReplacingMergeTree, migration 0003)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-016-metric-samples-and-headline-metrics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Keyed by tenant, CI, metric, versioned by ts and fed by a materialized view so a page of CIs reads its headlines with one primary-key IN query and argMax(value, ts)."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics_headline_metric_graphql", "label": "Ci.headlineMetric / HeadlineMetric batch loader (GraphQL 0.8.0)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-016-metric-samples-and-headline-metrics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Per-request batch loader asks ClickHouse once per page; runs in an OpenTelemetry span counted by openmap_clickhouse_queries_total. First ClickHouse dependency at API request time; an outage fails the field, not the page."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics_health_states", "label": "HEALTH_STATES", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-016-metric-samples-and-headline-metrics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics_synthetic_estate_samples", "label": "Synthetic estate emits headline samples", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-016-metric-samples-and-headline-metrics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every known-layer CI carries one headline sample per result, subnets add ipam.subnet.utilisation_percent and PDUs dcim.power.watts, from existing attributes (measuredKw) or the slot's deterministic RNG, so replaying fills metrics the way a real sweep would."}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics_ci_summary_fields", "label": "CI_SUMMARY_FIELDS selects headlineMetric", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-016-metric-samples-and-headline-metrics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics_req_cmdb_038", "label": "REQ-CMDB-038", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-016-metric-samples-and-headline-metrics.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics", "target": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics_metric_sample", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-016-metric-samples-and-headline-metrics.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics_metric_sample", "target": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics_metric_name_pattern", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/ADR-016-metric-samples-and-headline-metrics.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_adr_016_metric_samples_and_headline_metrics", "target": "docs_a